{
  "schema": "br-qbhs0-writer-sample-outside-serializer-ab-v1",
  "bead": "br-qbhs0",
  "author": "CopperGoose (Claude Opus 5.5)",
  "change_under_test": "db queries.rs create_message_with_recipients_impl: the writer's two post-commit COUNT queries run after MESSAGE_WRITE_SERIALIZER is released (they were ~10% of its hold at saturation per the br-qbhs0 attribution).",
  "decision_rule_fixed_before_the_run": "Writer post-commit sample outside MESSAGE_WRITE_SERIALIZER: A/B decision rule. Written 2026-10-11 ~17:55Z, before\nbuild17 finished and before any run.\n\nArms (release builds, same host, one invocation):\n  base   = build16/base, main 1a787eda\n  sample = 1a787eda + writer_sample_outside.patch: the two COUNT queries after commit run after the serializer\n           is released (~10% of its hold at saturation per the br-qbhs0 attribution)\n\nRuns: paced_swarm.py, 60 agents, 300 s.\n  - Period 2 s (saturating, where serializer capacity binds): base sample sample base base sample.\n  - Then period 6 s: sample base base sample.\n\nDecision, pooling every send of the runs per arm and period:\n  S1. Period 2 s: pooled sample send p50 and p90 are each at least 10% lower than pooled base's. Every sample\n      run's p50 is below the median of the base runs' p50s.\n  S2. Period 2 s: pooled send p99 is no more than 20% above base's. Send+fetch errors are no more than base's + 3.\n  S3. Period 6 s: pooled sample send p50 and p90 are no more than 10% above base's (no regression below\n      saturation).\n  S4. Correctness:\n      - db lib message_serializer_is_released_before_the_post_commit_probe passes; it is extended to assert\n        that writer samples run unlocked;\n      - db lib create_message tests pass;\n      - db clippy shows no findings in queries.rs beyond main's existing ones.\n  WIN if S1-S4 hold: it lands with this evidence. Otherwise it is not landed and the loss/null is reported.\n",
